No.  I did not estimate the number of potions of healing per level at
all.  I did a simple calculation assuming that by a certain level one
has found a certain number of potions or a certain number of potions has
been generated (that is the only point where I used the assumption of a
certain average number of potions per level) to obtain an estimate of
the probability for any number of potions of *healing obtained by that
time.  For this I needed the probability of occurrence of a potion of
*healing.  As the only number available to me was the probability of
generation on the floor I took that one, hoping it was not too far from
the overall probability of generation of potions of *healing.  This
assumption may have been wrong, as the discussion with Marc Hartstein
revealed, but the method of calculation remains valid.  Plug in the
right probability and you'll get the right answer.


